---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, CONTROLLER, ISSUES, DISCUSSIONS, POLICY_DATE } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Contact and grievances"
  description="How to reach the people behind PhonePad, and how privacy requests and grievances are handled."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)">Contact and grievances</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated {POLICY_DATE}.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A bug: <a href={ISSUES} rel="noopener">open an issue</a>.</li>
        <li>A question or an idea: <a href={DISCUSSIONS} rel="noopener">start a discussion</a>.</li>
        <li>Anything else, including privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Grievance Officer</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Grievance Officer, {CONTROLLER}</strong><br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=Grievance`}>{CONTACT}</a><br />
        Based in India.
      </p>
      <p>
        Handles complaints and requests about personal data on all DynShift
        sites: access, correction, erasure, withdrawal of consent, nomination,
        and anything else about how your data is handled.
      </p>

      <h2>How a request is handled</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Write to the address above, saying what you want done. For analytics,
          include your Google Analytics client identifier if you have it;
          nothing else identifies you there.
        </li>
        <li>You get an acknowledgement, and a full answer within <strong>30 days</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          We may ask for just enough to confirm the request is yours, and will
          never ask for a password or an identity document for this.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you are not satisfied: in India, you may complain to the Data
          Protection Board of India after this grievance process; in the EEA,
          the UK or Switzerland, to your data protection authority.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Requests about Google's advertising data are Google's to answer, through
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener nofollow">My Ad Center</a>
        and Google's own privacy tools.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
